      "card_ids": ["C01","C11","C04","C17","C18"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "All transferable human L1 contexts report F values or qualitative outcomes at or above about 50%: aprepitant 59-67%, tegoprazan 86-100%, rolipram 73%, balcinrenone 52%, d-fenfluramine 61-69%, SB-681323 about 50%, thalidomide 80-100%, and INS018_055 good oral bioavailability.",
      "card_ids": ["C03","C07","C10","C12","C21","C08","C05","C15","C13","C06","C02","C14","C09"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 Caco-2 records for structurally similar fused-lactam basic amines M01 and M03 show high permeability (>10 x 10^-6 cm/s) and low efflux ratios (2.27 and 1.75), and fexuprazan shows efflux ratio <2, indicating no gut-wall efflux barrier.",
      "card_ids": ["C53","C56","C55"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 human liver microsomal intrinsic clearance for M01, which shares the N-methyl benzylamine and indole amide/lactam features, is low (about 4-9 ml/min/kg with or without NADPH), supporting low hepatic first-pass; vonoprazan also has a low CLint value (2.73 µL/min/mg) alongside a conflicting higher value.",
      "card_ids": ["C58","C60","C61","C62","C64","C68","C67","C66"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The closest fused indole-lactam reference M03 has moderate-to-high HLM CLint (66 µL/min/mg) and moderate hepatocyte CLint, but this is not a direct F measurement and is not sufficient to establish F<20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C59","C63","C65"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No affirmative transferable F<20% evidence exists; L2 animal low-F records for rolipram are species-specific and do not transfer to the human-oriented prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C16","C19"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63","C64","C65","C66","C67","C68","C69"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule is present in the supplied records.",
    "No exact same-scaffold reference context is present; the closest structural contexts are safinamide and L5/L6 reference molecules M01/M03, but the query's fused indole-lactam differs from safinamide's simple benzylamine amide.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2 permeability, efflux, or intestinal metabolism data are supplied; L5 records are for reference molecules.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability data are supplied; L6 records are for reference molecules M01-M03 with mixed CLint values.",
    "Dose, formulation, and prandial-state effects for the query are unknown.",
    "L3/L4 records lack IV comparators and query-specific measurements, so they cannot quantify absolute F."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 hepatic-clearance evidence is mixed: M01 (sharing the N-methyl benzylamine/indole features) has low HLM CLint, while the closest fused indole-lactam M03 has moderate-to-high CLint; neither is a direct F result. Combined with all transferable human L1 F values >=50%, the closest structural context safinamide at ~95%, and L5 high permeability/low efflux for similar fused lactam basic amines, the prediction remains high with no affirmative F<20% evidence."
}

